From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thibaut Lapierre <root@epheo.eu>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/12] multinode: ovn interconnect zones

Upstream's multinode OVN cannot host CA-less workers: its master
DaemonSet needs the master label and its components use the kubeadmin
kubeconfig. Every node here is its own OVN interconnect zone instead:

- assets/components/ovn/zones/{master,node}: local nbdb, sbdb, northd and
  ovn-controller plus a combined zone controller (--zone $K8S_NODE) on
  every node; the master DaemonSet runs the cluster manager only.
- Service-account auth with apiserver= in ovnkube.conf (net.JoinHostPort,
  so IPv6 control planes work). The cluster manager keeps the controller
  account; zone pods get ovn-kubernetes-node-limited, the
  cluster-network-operator's node-limited role minus CSRs, since root on
  any worker holds that token: pods and nodes written through status only,
  ConfigMaps and leases in openshift-ovn-kubernetes only.
- The NB zone is named after the node in nbdb's postStart.
- Workers get their node IP as a host alias on br-ex and a route to the
  apiserver advertise address via the control plane.
- microshift-cleanup-data drops the OVN databases, which the zones keep
  on the host under /etc/openvswitch.

Community builds run multinode mode by default, so single-node installs
use these manifests too.
Covered by: vm-test (single node), multinode-smoke and multinode-test
(cross-node pod, service and DNS traffic).
